-- THE FINDINGS' EVIDENCE. Each section is one finding of NOTES.md section 4, named by its id (W1, W2, ...). A section
-- asserts the surprising answer the instrument gives. A finding that is only a reading of the text (NOTES.md says "reading
-- only") has no section here. V1 is pinned at 1 June 2025, V2 at 1 March 2026, V3 at 1 August 2026.

§ `Findings: evidence`

§§ `W1: the replaced Dieu 73 has no bar on carrying on insurance business before the date of official operation`

@@q 1377 1379
@@qa 40 68
@ref Dieu 73 (src:1377-1379; src:law139-2025-qh15:40-68)
@@fx `an insurer trading before its opening date` : `Preparation for official operation` ; `carried on insurance business before the date of official operation` = TRUE
-- V1 says it is a breach, V2 and V3 say the paragraph does not exist.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 73(4): the business before the date of official operation breaches Dieu 73(4)` `an insurer trading before its opening date`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 73(4): the business before the date of official operation breaches Dieu 73(4)` `an insurer trading before its opening date`)

§§ `W2: from 2028 to 2030 the V2 text has the capital adequacy ratio in force but not the supervisory measures, while Dieu 156(4) and old Dieu 77-81, 83, 98 run on`

@@qb 528 530
@@qa 292 304
@ref Dieu 156 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:528-530; src:law139-2025-qh15:292-304)
@@fx `an insurer at the control level` : `A supervisory measure` ; `the capital adequacy ratio is at the level that requires control` = TRUE
-- On 1 June 2029 the V1 text has the control measure in force; the V2 text does not (it starts on 1 January 2031).
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 113(1): the Ministry of Finance may order control measures` `an insurer at the control level` (YMD 2029 6 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 113(1): the Ministry of Finance may order control measures` `an insurer at the control level` (YMD 2029 6 1))
-- The capital adequacy ratio itself (Dieu 95) is in force from 2028 in both texts.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 95` (YMD 2029 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 110` (YMD 2029 6 1))
-- The old Law's Dieu 98 is in force on that day under the V2 text, not under the V1 text.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 156(3): the old Law provision is in force on the day` `old Dieu 98` (YMD 2029 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 156(3): the old Law provision is in force on the day` `old Dieu 98` (YMD 2029 6 1))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 156(4): the interim capital duty applies on the day` (YMD 2029 6 1))

§§ `W3: Dieu 153(1)(c) lets the Ministry ask banks about breaches of provisions that are not yet in force`

@@qb 473 483
-- On 1 June 2025 only Dieu 100 is wholly in force of the five cited provisions; Dieu 109 and 110 are not in force even in part.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 153(1)(c): the cited provision is wholly in force on the day` `Dieu 100` (YMD 2025 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 153(1)(c): the cited provision is at least partly in force on the day` `Dieu 109` (YMD 2025 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 153(1)(c): the cited provision is at least partly in force on the day` `Dieu 110` (YMD 2025 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 153(1)(c): the cited provision is wholly in force on the day` `Dieu 109` (YMD 2030 12 31))

§§ `W4: the repeal of Dieu 155 from 1 July 2026 says nothing of the Investment Law lines it added`

@@qb 516 522
@@qa 339 339
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 6 30) (`Dieu 155: the Law lists the business line as a conditional investment business line` `insurance brokerage`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 7 1) (`Dieu 155: the Law lists the business line as a conditional investment business line` `insurance brokerage`)

§§ `W5: V3 removes the conditions for supplying ancillary services (Dieu 143) and the bar on unqualified ancillary services (Dieu 9(3)), yet the Law still lets insurers, brokers and others supply them`

@@qb 259 286
@@qa 333 339
@ref Dieu 143 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:259-286; src:law139-2025-qh15:333-339)
@@fx `an unqualified ancillary provider` : `An act in insurance business` ; `is an ancillary insurance service` = TRUE ; `the actor does not meet the conditions of law to do it` = TRUE
@@fx `an adviser with no degree` : `A provider of ancillary services (conditions)` ; `is an individual giving advice` = TRUE ; `has full civil act capacity` = TRUE
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 9: the act is prohibited` `an unqualified ancillary provider`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 9: the act is prohibited` `an unqualified ancillary provider`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 143: the provider meets the conditions to supply ancillary services` `an adviser with no degree`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 143: the provider meets the conditions to supply ancillary services` `an adviser with no degree`)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 140: the provider may supply the service to the recipient` `an individual` `an insurer, reinsurer, foreign branch, broker or mutual organisation` `advice`)

§§ `W6: Dieu 35 sits in the section on life and health contracts but its words give a 21-day withdrawal to every contract of more than a year`

@@q 760 769
@ref Dieu 35 (src:760-769)
@@fx `a property contract of ten years` : `A contract of insurance` ; `class of contract` = `a property insurance contract` ; `insurer` = `a non-life insurer` ; `policyholder` = `an ordinary adult` ; `insured person` = `an ordinary adult` ; `first day of the insurance term` = YMD 2025 1 1 ; `last day of the insurance term` = YMD 2035 1 1
@@fx `an ordinary adult` : `A person`
@@fx `a withdrawal on day 10` : `A decision to withdraw` ; `date the policyholder received the contract` = YMD 2025 2 1 ; `date the policyholder refused to continue` = YMD 2025 2 11 ; `premium paid` = 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 35: the policyholder may refuse to go on` `a withdrawal on day 10` `a property contract of ten years`

§§ `W7: Dieu 26 names four grounds for either side to terminate but does not say which side may use which`

@@q 624 635
-- Read literally, a policyholder who stops paying premium is "entitled" to terminate for non-payment; the encoding reads the
-- ground 1 as the insurer's (fork F8) and this assertion shows the reading it takes.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 26: the party has the right to terminate on the ground` `premium not paid, or not paid in full, by the agreed time or after the grace period` `the policyholder`

§§ `W8: Dieu 58(1) can be read as an occurrence rule or a claims-made rule, and the two give opposite answers`

@@q 1083 1089
@ref Dieu 58 (src:1083-1089)
@@fx `a claim after the term for an act within it` : `A liability contract and a claim` ; `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` = TRUE ; `the act causing the damage occurred within the insurance term` = TRUE
@@fx `a claim within the term for an act before it` : `A liability contract and a claim` ; `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` = TRUE ; `the third person's claim was made within the insurance term` = TRUE
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` `a claim after the term for an act within it`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises (claims-made reading)` `a claim after the term for an act within it`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` `a claim within the term for an act before it`
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises (claims-made reading)` `a claim within the term for an act before it`

§§ `W9: Dieu 148(2) is silent on damage and liability contracts of a mutual organisation`

@@qb 358 361
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 148(2): the rules of Chuong II apply to the mutual organisation's contract of the class` `damage insurance contracts`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 148(2): the rules of Chuong II apply to the mutual organisation's contract of the class` `liability insurance contracts`

§§ `W10: Dieu 65(3) lets the Government fix the minimum total assets "for each period" on the basis of figures the Law itself states`

@@q 1211 1228
@ref Dieu 65 (src:1211-1228)
@@fx `a Vietnamese company with 2500 billion` : `A member of a limited liability insurer` ; `is an organisation` = TRUE ; `meets the general conditions of Dieu 64` = TRUE ; `total assets in the year before the application, in Vietnamese dong` = 2_500_000_000_000
@@fx `the same under a Government minimum of 3000 billion` : `A member of a limited liability insurer` ; `is an organisation` = TRUE ; `meets the general conditions of Dieu 64` = TRUE ; `total assets in the year before the application, in Vietnamese dong` = 2_500_000_000_000 ; `minimum total assets the Government specifies for the period` = JUST 3_000_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 65: the member of the limited liability insurer meets the conditions` `a Vietnamese company with 2500 billion`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 65: the member of the limited liability insurer meets the conditions` `the same under a Government minimum of 3000 billion`

§§ `W11: after Dieu 69 is repealed the 60 days of Dieu 70(1) still run from a complete and valid dossier the Law no longer describes`

@@q 1307 1309
@@qa 336 337
@ref Dieu 70 (src:1307-1309; src:law139-2025-qh15:336-337)
@@fx `a dossier received on 1 March 2026` : `A licence decision` ; `date the Ministry of Finance received the complete and valid dossier` = YMD 2026 3 1
@@fx `an empty dossier` : `A licence dossier`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 70(1): the last day for the Ministry of Finance to grant or refuse` `a dossier received on 1 March 2026`) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 69: the dossier contains the documents the Law lists` `an empty dossier`)

§§ `W12: Dieu 127(1): the V1 and V2 texts bar different pairs of principals`

@@q 2734 2743
@@qa 222 233
@ref Dieu 127 (src:2734-2743; src:law139-2025-qh15:222-233)
@@fx `a life insurer that also sells health, and a health insurer` : `Two engagements of an individual agent` ; `first principal` = `a life insurer` ; `second principal` = `a health insurer` ; `types of insurance the first principal carries on` = LIST `life insurance`, `health insurance` ; `types of insurance the second principal carries on` = LIST `health insurance`
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 127(1): the individual may not be the agent of both principals` `a life insurer that also sells health, and a health insurer`)
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 127(1): the individual may not be the agent of both principals` `a life insurer that also sells health, and a health insurer`)

§§ `W13: V2 drops "the right to manage an enterprise under the Law on Enterprises" from the general conditions of an officer, Dieu 81`

@@q 1549 1554
@@qa 79 85
@ref Dieu 81 (src:1549-1554; src:law139-2025-qh15:79-85)
