§§ `W14: the deposit of Dieu 96 is a percentage of the MINIMUM charter capital at establishment, so it does not grow with the insurer`

@@q 2028 2033
@ref Dieu 96 (src:2028-2033)
@@fx `an insurer that grew tenfold` : `A deposit` ; `minimum charter capital or minimum allocated capital at the time of establishment` = 300_000_000_000 ; `amount deposited` = 6_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 96(2): the deposit made is the amount the Law requires` `an insurer that grew tenfold`

§§ `W15: the reserve fund of Dieu 98 has no maximum in the Law, so the contribution cannot be computed from the Law alone`

@@q 2071 2075
@ref Dieu 98 (src:2071-2075)
@@fx `a fund with no maximum supplied` : `A reserve fund position` ; `after-tax profit of the year` = 100_000_000_000 ; `balance of the compulsory reserve fund` = 10_000_000_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 98(2): the contribution to the compulsory reserve fund for the year` `a fund with no maximum supplied`

§§ `W16: the Law counts "ngay" (days) without defining it, and uses "ngay lam viec" (working days) only in Dieu 117`

@@q 2559 2563
@ref Dieu 117 (src:2559-2563)
-- Seven days from Monday 3 March 2025: Monday 10 March if calendar days, Wednesday 12 March if working days.
@@fx `a regular item on Monday 3 March 2025` : `A disclosure event` ; `kind` = `regular information (Dieu 119)` ; `date the period for sending the report ended, or the event occurred` = YMD 2025 3 3
#ASSERT `Dieu 117(2): the last day to publish the information` `a regular item on Monday 3 March 2025` EMPTY EQUALS YMD 2025 3 12
#ASSERT (YMD 2025 3 3) PLUS 7 EQUALS YMD 2025 3 10

